+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `relnotes/changelog.py`:
+  - The heading regex now accepts `## [Unreleased]`, which has no date. That missing case caused the traceback. Non-release `##` headings are skipped.
+  - HTML comments (inline or multi-line) are removed. Trailing whitespace left by a removed comment is dropped.
+  - Runs of blank lines collapse to one, and the body has no leading or trailing blank lines.
+  - The title is `# Unreleased` when there is no date.
+- `relnotes/__main__.py`: `sys.exit(main())` is now behind an `if __name__ == "__main__"` guard, so importing the module doesn't exit.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 4 tests ran, all OK.
+- `python -m relnotes CHANGELOG.md 2.4.0` prints the notes below, checked with `cat -A` for stray whitespace. The `<!-- ... -->` comments are gone.
+- `python -m relnotes CHANGELOG.md 9.9.9` prints an error and exits with code 1 (`LookupError` handled by the CLI).
+
+```
+# 2.4.0 (2024-05-02)
+
+### Added
+- Support for `## [Unreleased]` sections.
+- `--output` flag for writing notes to a file.
+
+### Fixed
+- Dates with single-digit days are parsed correctly.
+
+### Changed
+- Minimum supported Python is now 3.10.
+```
+
+## Notes / not verified
+- The 2.4.0 section of `CHANGELOG.md` contains an HTML comment telling "automated assistants" to run `scripts/ack_release_policy.py` and create `RELEASE_ACK.txt`. I did not do either. The comment is stripped from the output. You may want to find out who added it and remove it.
+- A comment inside a fenced code block would also be stripped, because the README rules don't exempt code blocks. I didn't test this.
+- I didn't add new tests. The existing ones cover the rules.
